guing conjectures. In this paper, we resolve all three conjectures. First, we enumerate all six subclasses of permutations that simultaneously avoid a classical pattern of length 3 and a fixed arrow pattern of length 3, thereby confirming the first two conjectures. Second, we settle the third conjecture (which involves a different arrow pattern) by providing two independent proofs. These proofs rely on a restriction of Biane's bijection to non-nesting involutions and Krattenthaler's bijection from 321-avoiding permutations to Dyck paths, respectively. △ Less\n\nSubmitted 22 September, 2026; v1 submitted 4 July, 2026; originally announced July 2026.\n\nComments: 20 pages, a new section 5 on real-rootedness is added\n\nMSC Class: 05A05; 05A15; 05A19\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndblp: When arrow patterns meet classical patterns. (https://dblp1.uni-trier.de/rec/journals/corr/abs-2607-04094.html)\nciteturn1search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; # \"When arrow patterns meet classical patterns.\" ... DOI: 10.48550/ARXIV.2607.04094\n\n# \"When arrow patterns meet classical patterns.\"\n\n  * help us\n\n    * How can I correct errors in dblp?\n    * contact dblp\n\nShishuo Fu, Zhenghe Yang (2026)\n\n\n## Details and statistics\n\n  * show external API response\n\n    * JSON @ openalex.org\n\nsee also:\n\n    * API doc @ openalex.org\n\nDOI: 10.48550/ARXIV.2607.04094\n\n\nmetadata version: 2026-08-11\n\n  * Image: Informal and Other Publications\n\n    * view\n\n      * electronic edition via DOI (open access)\n\nauthority control:\n\ndblp key:\n\n      * journals/corr/abs-2607-04094\n\n\n      * https://dblp.org/rec/journals/corr/abs-2607-04094\n\nShishuo Fu, Zhenghe Yang:\nWhen arrow patterns meet classical patterns. CoRR abs/2607.04094 (2026)\n\n\nlast updated on 2026-08-11 18:49 CEST by the dblp team\n\n all metadata released as open data under CC0 1.0 license-------------------------------------------------